---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="How I Work | Fernando Alcantara Lopez" description="How Fernando Alcantara Lopez designs software, automates validation, and works with data and ML systems." path="/architecture">
  <main>
    <section class="page-intro mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-24" aria-labelledby="architecture-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">HOW I WORK</p>
      <h1 id="architecture-heading">Reliable systems start with clear thinking and careful validation.</h1>
      <p>I combine mathematical rigor, software discipline, and practical automation to build systems that are understandable and robust.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section-band mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6" aria-labelledby="capabilities-heading">
      <div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">01 / WHAT I DO</p><h2 id="capabilities-heading">The main parts of the work.</h2><p>Good boundaries help people move quickly without sacrificing quality or traceability.</p></div>
      <div class="capability-grid">
        <article class="capability-card"><span class="capability-number">01</span><h3>Software systems</h3><p>Build reliable Python and C++ tools for scientific, validation, and automation workflows.</p><div class="tag-row"><span>Python</span><span>C++</span><span>Automation</span></div></article>
        <article class="capability-card"><span class="capability-number">02</span><h3>Data pipelines</h3><p>Turn raw sensor data, model outputs, and evaluation results into understandable insights and repeatable workflows.</p><div class="tag-row"><span>ML</span><span>Computer Vision</span><span>ADAS</span></div></article>
        <article class="capability-card"><span class="capability-number">03</span><h3>Quality and validation</h3><p>Use testing, error analysis, and reproducible evaluation to reduce noise and improve decision quality.</p><div class="tag-row"><span>Validation</span><span>QA</span><span>Model Eval</span></div></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-band mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6" aria-labelledby="philosophy-heading">
      <div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">02 / PRINCIPLES</p><h2 id="philosophy-heading">Clarity beats cleverness.</h2><p>Good engineering decisions are easy to explain, test, and improve over time.</p></div>
      <div class="philosophy-panel"><p>I try to make the right way to change a system obvious and measurable.</p><ul class="philosophy-list"><li><strong>Clear</strong> — Small pieces, explicit assumptions, and readable logic.</li><li><strong>Testable</strong> — Automated checks and validation workflows that catch problems early.</li><li><strong>Evidence-based</strong> — Interpret data carefully and evaluate model behavior with real metrics.</li></ul><p>That matters in software, research, and validation work where small errors can lead to large consequences.</p></div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-band mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6" aria-labelledby="quality-heading">
      <div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">03 / CHECKS</p><h2 id="quality-heading">Let the tools catch the easy mistakes.</h2><p>Automation gives more time for the hard decisions and deeper analysis.</p></div>
      <div class="capability-grid"><article class="capability-card"><h3>Builds and tests</h3><p>Every workflow is validated through repeatable checks and targeted testing.</p></article><article class="capability-card"><h3>Data quality</h3><p>Model performance is reviewed against real data, edge cases, and error patterns.</p></article><article class="capability-card"><h3>Reproducibility</h3><p>Processes are designed to be reviewed, shared, and reproduced by others.</p></article></div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>